TITLE:Ship-wide Events Plan
H1:Ship-wide events: the Wren's big moments, in order <span class="draft">plan v4, for the user's approval</span>
SUB:Every ship-wide event (the "main missions"), in the order they happen from Day 0: what happens day by day, who speaks, what the news feed says, the jobs at each tier, what it does to the ship, and how it can go well or poorly. Built in Pillar 6, after Pillar 5's Step 4. v4 (2026-10-19) splits the work into two build phases and re-times the storm, Space Creature and Loss of Power; v3 put nine events inside the career arc; v2 applied the user's answers to v1. From the user's answers of 2026-10-18 (~23:25) and on v1, the design doc's "Ship-wide events", the Pillar 3 plan's list and the engine already in the game. Written by the Pillar 5 designer for lead 14.
NAV:v4=What changed in v4|phases=The two phases|plain=In plain words|rules=The user's rules|cal=The calendar|how=How every event works|list=The events|links=The links|engine=Changes to what's built|clash=Clashes|q=Open questions

<section id="v4">
  <h2>What changed in v4</h2>
  <p class="note"><b>The user (2026-10-19):</b> "Ion storm should be two days. 4 and 5. Give you your first full weekend free. Space creature pulls up a day and your test has more breathing room. Loss of power should stick you in the elevator for 4 game hours after your first meal. You will not be penalized for missing work. All the events [the nine in the career arc] are the ones we will make first. The others later."</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Ion storm: Days 4-5</b> (Thursday and Friday), two days: the all-clear on Friday evening. <b>Your first weekend (Days 6-7) has no event</b>: Sowing morning, film night's first night in the auditorium, rest.</li>
    <li><b>Space Creature: Day 8 only</b> (Monday), one day: the glow mid-morning, gone by 18:40, so there's a whole evening and night before your Day 9 test job. (Moving it a day earlier would put it in the free weekend, so it moved into one day instead: a short question at the bottom.)</li>
    <li><b>Loss of Power: four ship hours in the lift</b> (Day 24, 07:40-11:40), straight after breakfast. <b>Missed work isn't held against you:</b> no reputation lost, your jobs wait, and Calder says so.</li>
    <li><b>Two build phases:</b> <b>Phase 1</b> is the nine events inside the career arc (Days 1-26), built first; <b>Phase 2</b> is the other eleven, built later. Both are marked in the calendar and on each event.</li>
    <li>Settled and taken out of the questions: Space Creature straight after the storm (now Day 8, with the weekend between).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="phases">
  <h2>The two phases</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Phase 1 · built first</b><span>The nine events of the career arc, Days 1-26: the comet (2), the ion storm (4-5), Space Creature (8), the diplomatic visit (12-15), the power surge (17), Echo Signal (18), the distress call (21), Loss of Power (24), the Visiting Inspector (25).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag new">Phase 1</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Phase 2 · later</b><span>The other eleven, after the arc: the stowaway (31-33), crew rotation day (35), something in the garden (38-41), the late supply shuttle (45-46), the Wren cough (50-53), nebula drift (57-59), reactor trouble (64-66), salvage (73-75), a Veyli vessel needs help (80-81), the déjà vu day (87), the Founders' Day festival (100).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Phase 2</span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Phase 1 alone is a whole game: a 10-15 hour playthrough meets all nine. Until Phase 2 is built, the ship after Day 26 carries on with traditions, incidents and work, as it does after Day 100 anyway.</p>
</section>

<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Twenty events, each once.</b> Thirteen from the earlier plans, three new ones from the user's brainstorm (<b>the distress call, the stowaway, reactor trouble</b>) and four the user picked, inspired by Star Trek: The Next Generation (<b>Echo Signal, Loss of Power, the Visiting Inspector, Space Creature</b>; "that will be enough": no others), each pitched in full on <a href="events-pitch-tng.html">its own page</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Phase 1, built first: nine events during your career arc</b> (Days 1-26, the 10-15 hours most players have), around the big career moments. <b>Phase 2, later:</b> the other eleven, about one a week after the arc.</li>
    <li><b>Cozy and dangerous mixed</b> (the user: "both"); the dangerous ones can hurt someone a little (a day or two in the infirmary), never worse.</li>
    <li><b>You can't fail one,</b> and an event never costs you at work: every event ends; it goes smoothly, bumpily or roughly, told as story; something lasting stays either way.</li>
    <li><b>Your part grows with your rank:</b> as a junior you carry and fix, as an Officer you trace, as a Senior Officer you plan around people, as an Engine Specialist you lead a team with the bridge on the line.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="rules">
  <h2>The user's rules (binding)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Rule (2026-10-18)</th><th>What this plan does</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Events never repeat</td><td>Each happens once (the engine already works this way). After the last, the ship carries on with traditions, incidents and work; later pillars add new events.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Ion storm Day 4 or 5, 3 days, emergency lighting only at the start (2026-10-18); then two days, Days 4 and 5 (2026-10-19)</td><td>Days 4-5. Emergency lighting for about 20 minutes as it hits on Day 4; then flicker and faults only; the all-clear Friday evening.</td></tr>
