  </table></div>
  <p class="note">The days are fixed, so every game tells the same story, and they follow the ship's calendar, not your progress. An event that needs someone (Calder for the storm, Vance for the visit, Sato for the comet, the creature and the echo) moves a day if they're off. Inside the arc there's an event about every two or three days; the gaps are your first weekend (6-7) and the promotion days.</p>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <h2>How every event works (kept from the design doc)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Ambient:</b> never a mission you're given. News reaches you as it reaches everyone: chatter, the Ship app's <b>news feed</b> (with who told you), Mail, the boards, and at big turns the <b>Captain's address</b> on every deck. No cutscenes; the camera stays with you.</li>
    <li><b>Shape:</b> warning, onset, escalation, resolution, afterglow, over one to four days.</li>
    <li><b>Four kinds of moment:</b> felt everywhere, the Captain's address, gatherings at a real place and time, and meetings with dialogue (a panel of lines, sometimes two or three replies; walk away any time, the gist comes by Mail).</li>
    <li><b>Jobs by tier:</b> each event's jobs go on the board tagged with the event; you see the ones for your tier and below. The Tier 3 and Tier 4 rows are <b>slots</b>: the kind of work is named here, and Steps 5 and 6 of Pillar 5 (shutdowns, the night shift's senior post, the Monday briefing, leading a team, the reactor) give them their exact verbs.</li>
    <li><b>Threads and bands:</b> three to five threads per event, measured from what really happened; each lands smoothly, bumpily or roughly, and the blend is the result. Your own part (jobs done, meetings, people helped) is counted separately: your commendation, the friendships, a mention in the debrief.</li>
    <li><b>Traces:</b> something stays on the ship either way: a pinned roster, a plaque, a sculpture, a pet, a scorch mark.</li>
    <li><b>Traditions:</b> paused in an event's hardest phases (no quiz night in a storm), except birthdays; a party or gathering after.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="list">
  <h2>The events</h2>

  <h3 id="e-comet">1. Comet viewing <span class="tag">short · cozy · Day 2 (Tue evening), 1 evening · drafted (comet-viewing-draft.js) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A comet passes close enough to fill the bow windows with its tail. No strain at all: a gentle evening.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 2 Tue 08:00</time><span>Sato's Mail (your rounds with Torres that morning; Rina's health check and your first laundry after shift: the evening is free).</span></li><li><time>21:00-22:15</time><span>The comet at the bow lounge windows and in the observatory (Sato's scope): your first look at what's outside, and your first meeting with Sato before her storm.</span></li><li><time>Day 3</time><span>A little chatter at breakfast.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> none needed; Sato at the scope has a line for whoever takes a turn.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Comet at nine. Get a window seat early." · after: "Green all the way along the tail."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> mood up a little.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> always smooth: nothing to lose.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>(none; you can help Sato carry the folding chairs)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-storm">2. Ion storm <span class="tag">main · danger · Days 4-5 (Thu-Fri), 2 days · built (0.34.12), to be changed · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>Survey spots an ion front ahead that the Wren can't steer round. The ship rides it out for a day and a half: flickering lights, no calls home, a tired bridge. The first time you see the whole crew pull together, and it's over in time for your first weekend.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 4 Thu 06:00 · warning</time><span>Dr. Sato's readings; chatter starts in Survey. 08:15 <b>Calder's storm briefing</b> at the Works job board. <b>12:30 the first all-hands</b> (the Captain at the lectern in the auditorium: "We're heading into weather").</span></li><li><time>Day 4 Thu 14:00 · onset</time><span><b>Felt everywhere:</b> a jolt, every deck drops to <b>emergency lighting for about 20 minutes</b> (the only emergency lighting of the storm, the user's rule), then flickering. The Captain's address. Comms down: booths shut, no outside Mail. Bridge on double shifts; the bow lounge closes. Kovac cracks her elbow in the jolt (a day in the infirmary).</span></li><li><time>Day 5 Fri 06:00 · escalation</time><span>Power wear doubled, comms tripled: relay faults, the chiller strains (no more blackouts). Storm stew; trays to the bridge by cart. Crew short-tempered after a bad night.</span></li><li><time>Day 5 Fri 18:30 · resolution</time><span><b>The all-clear</b> in the observation room (a meeting) and on every deck. Comms back: a queue at the booths all evening. The Friday jam turns into the storm party in the bow lounge.</span></li><li><time>Days 6-7 · afterglow (no event)</time><span>Your free weekend. Chatter, the debrief Mail, commendations. Sowing morning on Saturday is the first calm morning, and Saturday's film night is the first in the auditorium. Vance's bridge invitation at Sunday breakfast (for bridge hour on Day 23) if you helped (see "The links").</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Calder's briefing (one choice: take the bridge battery run, the lounge, or nothing); the first all-hands; the all-clear (if you're there, the Captain thanks the Works crew by name).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Sato hasn't left the chart room since last night." · "They say it's the size of a moon." · "No calls home till it's over." · after: "Lights only went once, thanks to Works."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> power and comms dip hard on Days 4-5; food if the chiller strains; mood dips, then lifts at the party.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> short flicker, nothing spoiled, a cheerful party: <b>the storm crew's signed duty roster</b> pinned in the tea corner.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> long faults, binned food, a grumpy Friday night: a scorch mark and a taped panel in the relay room.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>secure the lounge glassware; shielded lamp ballasts; battery packs from Deck 5 to the bridge; trays to the bridge</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace a relay line that keeps tripping (the power line, once P5 exists; a flow fault on water/heat now)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot (Step 5):</i> plan which decks get power first if a junction goes; the bridge crew's rest rota</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot (Step 6):</i> lead the relay repair team with the bridge on the line</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-creature">3. Space Creature <span class="tag">main · cozy (wonder) · Day 8 (Mon), one day · NEW (TNG-inspired) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>The Monday after the storm, the power keeps dipping. Everyone blames storm damage, but Works can't find a fault. Then the port windows glow: a baby space creature, drawn in by the storm, has latched onto the hull near a power conduit and is feeding on the Wren's power. Nobody wants to hurt it. Works weans it off, a step at a time, and it's gone by dinner. (Pitched in full on <a href="events-pitch-tng.html#creature">its own page</a>.)</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 8 Mon 07:00 · warning</time><span>Small power dips with no fault ("the storm's last hiccups"); the lights soften during the Monday briefing.</span></li><li><time>09:20 · onset</time><span><b>Felt everywhere:</b> a soft glow drifts across every port-side window. Sato: "It's alive. And it's young." The Captain's address at 09:40: "We have a visitor. We're going to be gentle."</span></li><li><time>10:00-17:00 · escalation</time><span>Sato, Calder and Torres's plan at the Works board (a short meeting): lower the hull conduit's output a notch at 11:00, 13:00, 15:00 and 17:00 (tuning, M5's verb). Your first small incident and your uniform are that day too; the weaning steps are short and optional. Crew name it at lunch ("Sprat" leads the vote).</span></li><li><time>18:40 · resolution</time><span><b>It lets go and swims off</b> as the mess sits down to dinner; far out, a larger glow comes to meet it (felt everywhere: every window). Applause in the mess. Full power, a free evening and a night's sleep before your test job.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Sato and Calder's plan at the Works board (a meeting); the Captain's address; Sato at the observatory scope at lunch.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "The power's dipping and Works can't find why." · "There's something ON the hull." · "They're calling it Sprat." · after: "Its mother came for it. I cried, I don't mind saying."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> power a little low for the day (lights soft, the galley slower); mood up.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> <b>"Sprat" in the ship's log</b> and Sato's sketch of it framed in the observatory; it left on its own, unhurt.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> it took till late evening: a scorched hull plate where it fed (a job for later); it still swims off safe.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>hand lamps where the lights are low; carry readings from the conduit panel to Sato</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace where on the power line it's drawing from (P5)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan who gets power while the output's down (the infirmary, air)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead the weaning steps with the bridge holding the ship still</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-visit">4. Diplomatic visit <span class="tag">main · cozy (social) · Days 12-15 (Fri-Mon morning), 2 days aboard · built as a draft (0.34.16), to be shortened · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A Veyli delegation of four (Speaker Teshavi, her aide Kesrin, the scholar Moleth, their pilot Ithra) spends a weekend aboard. The Veyli like it warm, love herbs and notice manners.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 12 Fri 09:00 · warning</time><span>Vance's Mail; Holt grumbles. Get the visitors' suite and second cabin ready (heaters up), fix the Captain's dining lamp, carry gift crates from the hold; dress uniforms through the laundry.</span></li><li><time>Day 13 Sat 10:00 · onset</time><span><b>The greeting</b> in the shuttle bay (a meeting): the crew line the bay; if you're near the front a delegate speaks to you. 19:30 the formal dinner (a meeting for the table).</span></li><li><time>Day 14 Sun · escalation and resolution</time><span>The tea ritual in the observatory, a tour of the decks, Holt and the pilot's small clash (gossip). 11:00 <b>the gift exchange</b> in the observation room. The guests stay for <b>talent night</b> (Day 14) that evening.</span></li><li><time>Day 15 Mon 07:30 · farewell</time><span>A short farewell at the shuttle bay before the day shift; afterglow that day.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the greeting (courteous replies nudge the courtesy thread); the dinner (Tier 3+ at the table); the gift exchange.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Veyli on Saturday. Heaters up on Deck 2." · "Holt and their pilot had words about the Watch rota." · after: "The Speaker asked after the junior who fixed her lamp."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> heat on Deck 2 (cold cabins hurt); food (herbs, dinners on time); laundry load.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> a <b>Veyli cord sculpture</b> on the bow lounge's west wall (already built); Saruth warms to you.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> a stiff farewell, no gift; Holt's line becomes a running joke.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>heaters, lamps, gift crates, extra laundry, herbs from the garden to the galley</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace a cold cabin on Deck 2 (the heat line)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the tour route and who's on show; the dinner rota</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> at the Captain's table; brief the bridge on the Veyli shuttle's docking</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-surge">5. Power surge <span class="tag">short · danger · Day 17 (Wed), an afternoon · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A junction on Deck 6 trips under a surge and two decks lose power for a while.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 17 Wed 11:20</time><span><b>Felt everywhere:</b> a bang below, two decks dark (emergency lighting on those two decks). The morning of your power lesson (M19): Calder takes you straight there.</span></li><li><time>11:30-15:00</time><span>The Works crew on Deck 6; hand lamps; the galley on half power.</span></li><li><time>15:00</time><span>Power back; Calder's short Mail; the Captain's table toast goes ahead that evening.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Calder on the Works channel (a short briefing at the board).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Decks 4 and 5 are dark!" · after: "Junction 6-2 again. Torres says it's the last time."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> power down hard for hours; transport (the lift) slow.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> under two hours dark: a thank-you on the board.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> five hours: a tired evening, a scorched junction cover.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>hand lamps to the dark decks, battery packs to the infirmary</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace which machine on the power line dropped (P5, Step 5)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan who gets power back first (Tier 3, M18 shutdowns)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-echo">6. Echo Signal <span class="tag">short · cozy (moving) · Day 18 (Thu evening), 1 evening · NEW (TNG-inspired) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A drifting probe's faint signal turns out to carry music: a recording from the colony of Halden, lost before most of the crew were born. Survey cleans it up, and the whole ship gathers to listen.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 18 Thu 09:00 · warning</time><span>Sato's team picks up a signal under the noise; by lunch the word is "music". Chatter all afternoon.</span></li><li><time>16:00 · onset</time><span>The comms crew ask Works for a quieter line: the array's coolant hum is in the recording (a job).</span></li><li><time>20:30 · the gathering</time><span><b>The observation room on Deck 1</b>: the lights low, the crew on the floor and the steps, Sato plays the cleaned-up recording: a choir and a piano, then a child counting in. Silence after; then the Captain says a few words about Halden.</span></li><li><time>Day 19 · afterglow</time><span>People humming it at breakfast. The music room's piano has a new piece in the late piano tradition from then on.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Sato before it plays; the Captain's few words; a friend beside you afterwards (a choice: say how it felt, or just sit).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Sato found music in a probe signal." · "Halden. My gran used to talk about Halden." · after: "Someone's been playing it on the piano all night."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> comms (the array) for a day; mood up, quiet and warm.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> the whole tune recovered: <b>the Halden tune</b> joins the music room piano's pieces (late piano plays it), and Sato frames the probe's call sign.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> only half recovered: the piano plays a fragment, and crew hum the rest their own way.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>carry chairs, fix the observation room's speaker (a lamp-and-relay job)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the array coolant line's hum out of the comms (the heat line, M9)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-distress">7. Distress call <span class="tag">main · danger · Days 21-22 (Sun-Mon), 1 day and an afterglow · NEW, inside the career arc · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A beacon: a damaged courier pod, drifting, its air running low. The Tern flies out for the first time while you're aboard, brings the pod's pilot home, and the whole ship looks after someone it never met.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 21 Sun 11:30 · warning</time><span>Your Sunday off after the night shift. The bridge picks up the beacon; the Captain's address: "We're going to get them." Short warning: an hour.</span></li><li><time>12:30 · onset</time><span><b>The Tern launches</b> (the bay doors open; crew watch from the booth and the lobby window). The infirmary readied. The pilot's voice on the bay speaker, thin and calm.</span></li><li><time>14:30 · escalation</time><span>The pod is damaged and towing is slow; the Tern's air runs tight; the bay's doors must cycle on time. A second address.</span></li><li><time>16:30 · resolution</time><span><b>The Tern back in the bay</b> (a gathering): the pilot, Ilse Varga, helped out, wrapped in a blanket, a sprained wrist strapped, and a sack of undelivered mail she wouldn't leave behind.</span></li><li><time>Days 22-27 · afterglow</time><span>Ilse two days in the infirmary (a sprain and the cold), then a Deck 4 guest cabin until the Day 35 shuttle. Monday is your Tier 4 test, so nothing is asked of you; on Saturday (Day 27), a meeting in her guest cabin: Ilse thanks whoever helped. Her mail sack is sorted and sent on.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the bay speaker (Ilse and the Tern's pilot); the Captain's two addresses; Ilse in the infirmary (choices: ask about the pod, or just sit with her).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "There's a pod out there. One person." · "The Tern's going out!" · "She brought the mail with her. All of it." · after: "Ilse's in the guest cabin by the lift. She likes the garden."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> air and hull (the bay cycling), transport (the Tern), the infirmary's load; mood up at the end.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> Ilse always comes home (hurt a little, never badly). Smooth: <b>the pod's nameplate</b> on the shuttle bay wall, a friend in the guest cabin, Mail from Ilse later.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> Rough: a long cold wait, a dent in the bay door's seal (a job for later), Ilse quieter; still home, still grateful.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>carry blankets and med kits to the bay, top up the Tern's oxygen cells, sort the mail sack</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the bay's air line before the doors cycle (the air line, M9)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the bay clearance and the infirmary's night rota; who works the extra shift</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead the bay team with the bridge on the line (the approach and the door cycle)</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-stuck">8. Loss of Power <span class="tag">short · cozy-tense (people) · Day 24 (Wed), 07:40-11:40, four ship hours · NEW (TNG-inspired) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>A relay on the spine's power feed fails just after breakfast, and the lifts stop with the lights in the shaft. You're in the main lift with an odd little group: Chef Brennan with a crate of eggs, Nell (eight, a passenger's daughter, aboard for the week) and Commander Vance. Four hours: you fix what you can from inside; the ship fixes the rest from outside. <b>Missing work isn't held against you.</b> (Pitched in full on <a href="events-pitch-tng.html#power">its own page</a>.)</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 24 Wed 07:40 · onset</time><span>After your first meal of the day, you head for the lift; someone calls "Hold the doors!" and you step in. It stops between Decks 3 and 4; the car's small emergency lamp comes on; every lift stops (felt everywhere). (If you skip breakfast, it's the first lift you take that morning; if you never ride one, you help from outside: the spine ladder and the roof hatch.)</span></li><li><time>07:50-09:30 · escalation</time><span>Torres on the intercom: "It's the spine relay, and it's cooked. This'll take a while." Inside: reset the car's relay with your tool roll (a work step), which gets the fan and the light back; keep Nell calm; Brennan's eggs; Vance's story. Calder on the intercom: "Your board will keep. Nobody's counting this against you."</span></li><li><time>09:30-11:30 · the long middle</time><span>It gets warm and slow. Nell naps, then gets scared. Brennan's boiled eggs become breakfast-again. I-spy, a song, a game of twenty questions with Vance (who is terrible at it). The conversations go deeper.</span></li><li><time>11:40 · resolution</time><span>Works outside fits a new spine relay; your reset lets the car creep down to Deck 3; the doors open to applause. Nell insists on lunch with the four of you, so you do.</span></li><li><time>Afternoon · afterglow</time><span>Your morning's jobs are still on the board, no harm done; the reactor permit (M23) happens after lunch instead. Gossip ("Vance did impressions!").</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the four hours are a meeting in the car, in stretches: five or six choices (comfort Nell, ask Vance about his first ship, help Brennan save the eggs, sing, keep quiet); each nudges that friendship.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "All the lifts stopped!" · "Brennan's been in one since breakfast. With eggs." · "Four hours! Torres says the relay was cooked." · after: "Nell says the junior from Works is her best friend now."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> transport down for four hours (the morning's carts and jobs slow, crew on ladders, lunch carried up by hand).</li><li><b>No penalty:</b> work you missed while stuck doesn't count against you: no reputation lost, no missed-shift note, the jobs wait; anything urgent goes to the crew outside.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> <b>a big friendship boost</b> with all three (a full step each); Nell's drawing of "the lift people" on the Works bay board; Brennan's Lift Eggs on the menu from then on.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> a long, hot, cross four hours; still friends after (a smaller step).</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>inside: reset the car's relay, keep everyone calm; outside: ladders, hand lamps, the stairs</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace which relay on the lift's power line failed (the power line, P5)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the ladders and who carries meals up and down while the lifts are out</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead the lift-shaft team with the bridge (transport)</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-inspector">9. Visiting Inspector <span class="tag">main · cozy-tense · Day 25 (Thu), one day · NEW (TNG-inspired; shortened in v3) · <b>Phase 1</b></span></h3>
  <p>Fleet Inspector Dagny Krell comes aboard for a one-day audit: logs, a drill, machines, the job board, and the first team job you lead. Chief Holt is nervous, Calder is calm in a way that worries everyone, and Works scrambles to clear the board.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 24 Wed 16:00 · warning</time><span>Vance's Mail: an inspection, tomorrow. Holt drills the Watch that evening. The job board's backlog suddenly matters.</span></li><li><time>Day 25 Thu 08:00 · onset</time><span>The inspector off the early shuttle (a short meeting at the bay); her clipboard. She walks the decks with Vance and asks crew questions (yours: about a machine you really serviced).</span></li><li><time>10:00-14:00 · escalation</time><span><b>She watches your first team job as its lead</b> (M24, that morning anyway); a surprise drill at 13:00 (you run the Works part); she reads the logbook and inspects the galley.</span></li><li><time>16:00 · resolution</time><span><b>Her findings</b> in the observation room (a meeting), department by department, short and fair; she leaves on the evening shuttle. Calder's question at Friday tea the next day can mention them.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the inspector's question to you (choices: the honest detail, a confident summary, or "I'll check and come back": each fine, each a different note on her clipboard); her findings; Holt's relief.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "An inspector. Tomorrow." · "Holt's polishing the Watch office door." · "She opened the oven." · after: "Works got a line to itself in the findings."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> every system checked; a little extra wear from the rush; mood tense, then up.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> impressed: <b>a framed fleet commendation</b> for Works in the Works bay, and a line about you in her findings.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> embarrassed: a "notice of improvement" pinned in the Works bay, which the crew joke about for weeks; never a failure, never a punishment.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>clear the backlog, tidy and label the stores, clean the Works bay</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace a flaky line before she finds it</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the drill and the rota so the board is staffed while crew are questioned</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> walk her through the engine room with the bridge</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-stowaway">10. Stowaway <span class="tag">main · cozy (people) · Days 31-33 (Wed-Fri), 3 days · NEW · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>Unloading the Wednesday delivery, someone finds a person curled up behind the crates: Pip Arden, nineteen, who hid aboard at the supply depot because she wanted to see the stars. The ship has to decide what to do with her.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 31 Wed 10:15 · onset (no warning)</time><span><b>Found in the hold</b> during the delivery (you, if you're unloading; else Yara Esposito finds her and calls you over). Holt's Watch take her to the infirmary first.</span></li><li><time>Day 31 afternoon · escalation</time><span>Holt's questions in the Watch office (a meeting). Gossip everywhere. Pip in a guest cabin; nobody is sure if she's in trouble.</span></li><li><time>Day 32 Thu · escalation</time><span>Pip works a day in the galley with Brennan (she's good at it). The Captain asks for views: <b>a meeting in the ready room</b> with Vance, Holt and Brennan (Tier 3+ at the table; Tier 1-2 can speak up for her by Mail).</span></li><li><time>Day 33 Fri 09:00 · resolution</time><span>The Captain's decision, in an address: Pip works her passage in the galley and goes home on the next supply shuttle (Day 46). She always leaves. Afterglow: Pip in the mess, nervous and grinning; her goodbye at the shuttle on Day 46.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> finding her (choices: "Are you all right?" / call the Watch / give her your lunch: all good, each a different first line from her); Holt's questions; the ready room.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "There's someone in the hold!" · "She hid in a crate of flour. A crate of flour." · "Holt's not happy." · after: "Pip's on the galley line. Ask for extra."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> air in the hold (a fault found); mood: curious, kind.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> Pip leaves happy, with Brennan's apron and a letter of recommendation; <b>her drawing of the Wren</b> stays pinned in the galley, and a letter from her arrives a few weeks later.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> Pip leaves subdued; her letter comes later and is kind anyway. Never punished.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>clear and check the hold, make up a guest bunk, fetch clothes and a badge from stores</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the hold's stale air (how did she breathe? a damper on the air line)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan where she sleeps and works; the galley rota</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> the report to the depot with the bridge</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-rotation">11. Crew rotation day <span class="tag">short · cozy · Day 35 (Sunday) · uses the crew rotation already in the game · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>The Sunday shuttle takes crew home and brings new faces; the first rotation of your time aboard (the roster's Day 35 rotation).</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 34 Sat evening</time><span>The farewell supper (already a tradition).</span></li><li><time>Day 35 Sun 10:00</time><span>Goodbyes in the shuttle bay (a gathering); the new hand walks down the ramp. Ilse Varga leaves on this shuttle too.</span></li><li><time>Day 35-36</time><span>The new hand's tea (already a tradition); new names in Crew.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the leaver's goodbye to their friends (if you know them, a line to you).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Theo's going home on Sunday." · "There's a new one in Bunk 3."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> none; mood a little bittersweet.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> always smooth.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>carry the leavers' bags; make up the new hand's bunk</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> rework the rota for the gap</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-garden">12. Something in the garden <span class="tag">main · cozy (mystery) · Days 38-41 (Thu-Sun), 4 days · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>Nibbled leaves, a stripped herb rack, tiny tracks. Someone (something) is eating the garden. The crew blame each other until it's caught: a small harmless creature that stays as the ship's pet.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 38 · warning</time><span>Nibbles, tracks, things moved in storage; blame in chatter.</span></li><li><time>Day 39 · onset</time><span>The herb wall bare; Brennan's furious Mail; the menu goes bland.</span></li><li><time>Day 40 · escalation</time><span>Sightings on other decks; traps from the machine shop; a volunteer garden watch at night (a sign-up sheet).</span></li><li><time>Day 41 · resolution</time><span>Caught: a gathering in the garden, someone names it (a vote you can join).</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Brennan's rant; the naming (your suggestion can win).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Something ran under the bunks in Bunk 6!" · "Brennan's blaming the Watch." · after: "It sleeps in the tomato bed."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> food (crop loss, bland meals); mood dips then lifts.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> always gets a pet: <b>the ship's pet</b> lives in the garden for the rest of the game. How well it went decides how soon the garden recovers.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> the garden takes two weeks to recover; a bland fortnight.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>make and set traps, check them each morning, the garden watch</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace why the garden's humidity is high (the water line's irrigation)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the watch rota</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-late">13. The late supply shuttle <span class="tag">short · cozy-hard · Days 45-46 (Wed-Thu) · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>The Wednesday delivery doesn't come. Rationing, a bland menu, short filters, a busy machine shop. All from the numbers.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 45 Wed 10:00</time><span>No shuttle; Yara's Mail; a shortage list.</span></li><li><time>Day 45-46</time><span>Rationing; the machine shop makes parts.</span></li><li><time>Day 46 Thu 16:00</time><span>The shuttle arrives late; a double unload; Pip the stowaway goes home on it.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Yara at the stores counter.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "No delivery. Yara's counting filters." · after: "Two weeks of crates in one afternoon."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> food and stores low for two days.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> nobody goes without: Yara's thanks.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> a bland, grumpy two days.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>the double unload; parts made in the machine shop</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> decide what gets the last filters</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-cough">14. The Wren cough <span class="tag">main · cozy-hard · Days 50-53 (Mon-Thu), 4 days · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>A cough goes round. About a fifth of the crew are off, the infirmary fills, and the ship runs short-handed.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 50 · warning</time><span>Coughing in the mess; Rina mentions it.</span></li><li><time>Day 51 · onset</time><span>The infirmary fills; one bunk room quarantined.</span></li><li><time>Day 52 · escalation</time><span>Works short-handed; soup to the bunk rooms by cart; you can catch it if your hygiene is low (energy drains faster, nothing worse).</span></li><li><time>Day 53 · resolution</time><span>The last patients out; Rina and Dr. Nandakumar exhausted (bring them tea: a favour).</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Rina at the infirmary door; Dr. Nandakumar's Mail.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Half of Bunk 2 is coughing." · "Soup again." · after: "Rina slept for fourteen hours."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> every system a little (fewer hands); air in the infirmary.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> few caught it, nothing left undone: a thank-you card on the infirmary door.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> a long week, a backlog of jobs; recovers.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>soup carts, fresh linen, more jobs left for you on the board</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the infirmary's air (the air line)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> cover the gaps in the rotas (Tier 3: planning around people)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead a short-handed team job</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-nebula">15. Nebula drift <span class="tag">main · cozy (strange) · Days 57-59 (Mon-Wed), 3 days · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>The Wren drifts through a nebula. Every window fills with colour; crew dream strange dreams and talk late into the night.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 57 · warning</time><span>A visiting scientist arrives (Deck 4 guest cabin); the observatory booked.</span></li><li><time>Day 58 · onset</time><span><b>Felt everywhere:</b> every window fills with colour. The sensor array overloads.</span></li><li><time>Day 58-59 · escalation</time><span>Strange dreams (energy refills slower) and chatty crew (social faster); dream gossip; the observatory full every night.</span></li><li><time>Day 59 · resolution</time><span>The ship drifts out; the scientist's talk in the auditorium (a gathering).</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the scientist's talk; a dream told to you by a friend.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "I dreamt the Admiral could talk." · after: "Sato's printing the nebula."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> comms (the array); energy down, social up.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> <b>a framed print of the nebula</b> in the observatory.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> the print, and a tired ship for a day.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>carry coolant to the array</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the array's coolant line</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot (Step 5):</i> the sensor array's jobs (M20)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-reactor">16. Reactor trouble <span class="tag">main · danger · Days 64-66 (Mon-Wed), 2-3 days · NEW · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>A reading on the reactor that Torres doesn't like at 02:00. By morning the reactor is stepped down to low power, Deck 6 is cleared, and the ship runs on batteries while the Works crew find the fault. A real scare that ends well, because Works gets it right.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 64 Mon 02:10 · warning</time><span>The night engine watch calls Torres; the reactor alarm on Deck 6 only. By 06:00 rumours everywhere.</span></li><li><time>06:30 · onset</time><span><b>The Captain's address</b>: the reactor goes to low power "as a precaution". <b>Felt everywhere:</b> the lights step down to half; the lift slows; the galley on reduced power. Deck 6 cleared except the engine crew.</span></li><li><time>Day 64-65 · escalation</time><span>The fault traced to a coolant loop and a control-rod drive. A repair under permit, timed with the bridge (the helm holds the ship steady). A second address at the worst moment: a pressure spike, then calm. Saad Salo burns his hand on a valve: a day in the infirmary.</span></li><li><time>Day 65 evening · resolution</time><span><b>Full power</b>: the lights come back up deck by deck (felt everywhere). The Captain's all-clear names the Works crew.</span></li><li><time>Day 66 Wed · afterglow</time><span>The engine crew's party in the bow lounge; commendations.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Torres at the Deck 6 door (if you're there); a briefing in the Works bay with Calder and Torres; the bridge call during the repair (Tier 4: you're on it); the all-clear.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Torres was up at two." · "They've stepped the reactor down. It's fine. Probably." · "The lights are half." · after: "Works got it. Coolant loop, they said."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> power at half for a day and a half; transport (lift); food (reduced galley); air steady; mood dips hard, then the best party of the year.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> always ends well. Smooth: <b>the engine crew's signed valve wheel</b> on the Works bay wall, and the ship talks about Works for a week.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> Rough: two days at half power, a cold, tired ship; a scorch on the shielding; still fixed, still thanked.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>battery packs to the infirmary and galley, hand lamps, coolant seals and spare parts to Deck 6's door</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace the coolant loop's low flow (the heat line, M9)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot (Step 5):</i> plan who gets power while it's low (the infirmary, air, the galley), warn crew, the shutdown windows (M18)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot (Step 6):</i> lead the reactor team with the bridge: the permit, the dosimeter, the timed repair (M23-M24)</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-salvage">17. Salvage <span class="tag">main · cozy (adventure) · Days 73-75 (Wed-Fri), 3 days · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>Survey finds a derelict. The Tern flies out again and comes back with crates of odd finds.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 73 · warning</time><span>The derelict found; chatter about what it might be.</span></li><li><time>Day 74 · onset</time><span>The Tern out (a gathering at the bay's booth).</span></li><li><time>Day 74-75 · escalation</time><span>Crates fill the hold: sorting (cart jobs); one holds an old but excellent part.</span></li><li><time>Day 75 · resolution</time><span>A "salvage auction" evening in the bow lounge.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Survey's briefing; the auction (bid on an odd object for your cabin).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "It's old. Older than the Wren." · after: "Torres has a part he won't stop polishing."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> stores up.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> <b>the salvaged part</b> makes one machine wear slower for good; an odd object on a shelf.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> the part, but fitted late.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>sort crates, cart them to stores</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>fit the salvaged part (a Tier 2 machine)</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> plan the hold's space</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead the boarding team (later: away jobs)</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-veyli">18. A Veyli vessel needs help <span class="tag">short · danger · Days 80-81 (Wed-Thu) · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>A Veyli ship limps alongside; Works sends parts across; one Veyli engineer comes aboard for a few days. A seed for away jobs later.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 80</time><span>Their hail; Saruth translates (a meeting on the bridge for Tier 4).</span></li><li><time>Day 80-81</time><span>Parts across by the Tern; the engineer aboard (a guest).</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Saruth and the Veyli engineer (who remembers the visit if it went well).</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Veyli, limping." · after: "Their engineer beat Torres at tiles."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> stores down a little.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> a Veyli tool on the Works bay wall.</li><li><b>Goes poorly:</b> a stiff thank-you.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>pick and pack the parts</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>trace their fault from the readings they send</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> what we can spare</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td><i>slot:</i> lead the parts transfer with the bridge</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-dejavu">19. The déjà vu day <span class="tag">main · strange · Day 87 (Wed), replayed once · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>You wake to the same morning as yesterday. Only you (and perhaps Envoy Saruth) notice. What you change the second time changes how the day goes.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 86 midnight</time><span>A faint shimmer at the windows.</span></li><li><time>Day 87 (the replay)</time><span>The same breakfast, chatter and jobs; fix a fault early, warn a friend.</span></li><li><time>Day 87 evening</time><span>Survey finds the cause; the day runs on.</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> Saruth's hint ("Again, cadet?").</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Did breakfast feel... familiar?" · after: nobody else remembers.</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> as the day goes.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> a quiet line in your Record that only you understand.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>whatever you set right the second time</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>

  <h3 id="e-festival">20. Founders' Day festival <span class="tag">short · cozy (big crowd) · Day 100 (Tue, Founding Day), 1 day · designed (Pillar 3) · <b>Phase 2</b></span></h3>
  <p>The year Founding Day grows into a festival: the plaza decorated, the galley's big feast, the whole crew together. The crowd test, built once the phone test says over 70 crew in one place is fine.</p>
  <ol class="steps"><li><time>Day 99</time><span>Setting up the plaza (a sign-up sheet).</span></li><li><time>Day 100 Tue 17:00-22:00</time><span>The festival on the plaza and the feast; the Captain's words at 19:30 (the Founding Day tradition, made big).</span></li></ol>
  <ul><li><b>Dialogue:</b> the Captain's toast.</li><li><b>News feed:</b> "Bunting on the plaza already." · after: "Best feast since I came aboard."</li><li><b>Ship health:</b> food (the feast); mood up.</li><li><b>Goes well:</b> always smooth: the festival bunting stays a week.</li></ul>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Jobs</th></tr><tr><td>Tier 1 · fetch and fix</td><td>set up the plaza, lights and tables</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2 · trace</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3 · plan around people</td><td><i>slot:</i> the rota so the night shift gets a plate</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4 · lead with the bridge</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div></section>

<section id="links">
  <h2>The links (the lead's brief)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The first all-hands is the storm's:</b> Day 4, 12:30, in the auditorium on the rec dec (the rec dec plan already says the first all-hands comes with the first ship-wide event, not on Day 1); the mess hall until the rec dec is built. After it, an all-hands once a season plus event addresses.</li>
    <li><b>Film night moves after it:</b> its first night in the auditorium is Day 6 (Saturday), the evening after the storm's all-clear; every Saturday film night is there from then on.</li>
    <li><b>The bridge invitation comes from helping in the storm</b> (the user: keep the first bridge hour on Day 23): if you did a storm job, or were at Calder's briefing or the all-clear, Vance asks you at breakfast on Day 7 (Sunday) to bridge hour on Day 23; the Calendar and an appointment remind you the day before. If you sat the storm out, the invitation waits for the first event you help in, and the bridge hour after it.</li>
    <li><b>Commendations</b> (built): two event jobs, or one and a meeting: a letter from the Captain, and the ready room summons after your first.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="engine" class="builder">
  <h2>Changes to what's built (for the events engineer, Pillar 6)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>SHIP_EVENTS.ionStorm</code>: <code>days: 6 → 2</code> (Days 4-5; the afterglow is chatter and Mail only, no event days), <code>earliest: 10 → 4</code>, <code>spread: 0</code>; phases Day 4 06:00 (warning), Day 4 14:00 (onset), Day 5 06:00 (escalation), Day 5 18:30 (resolution), Day 5 23:00 (afterglow); <code>'blackouts'</code> moves to onset only, all decks for about 20 minutes; a meeting for the all-hands; the party is the Friday jam in the bow lounge; need stays Calder.</li>
    <li><code>SHIP_EVENTS.diplomatic</code>: <code>days: 9 → 4</code>, <code>earliest: 12</code>; the greeting Saturday 10:00, the dinner Saturday 19:30, the gift exchange Sunday 11:00, the farewell Monday 07:30; guests aboard Saturday to Monday.</li>
    <li><b>Phase 1 first:</b> <code>EVENT_ORDER</code> gets the nine Phase 1 events; Phase 2's eleven are added when they're built (each a block of data, so adding them later changes nothing that's there).</li>
    <li><code>EVENT_ORDER</code> (in the end): all twenty in this page's order, each with a fixed <code>earliest</code> day, <code>spread: 0</code> and <code>gap: 0</code>. Events may now be a day apart or on consecutive days (the surge and the echo, Loss of Power and the inspector), so <code>eventDueDay</code> takes the fixed day even when the last event ended the day before.</li>
    <li>The comet: <code>plans/comet-viewing-draft.js</code> as it is, <code>earliest: 2</code> (it was drafted to follow the storm; it now comes before it, which the draft's <code>gap</code> already allows once it's first in <code>EVENT_ORDER</code>).</li>
    <li>New blocks: <code>distress</code> (the Tern's launch: the bay doors' moment, built first here, reused by salvage), <code>stowaway</code> (a guest, leaves on Day 46's shuttle), <code>reactor</code> (low power through section 17's effects), <code>echo</code> (one gathering; the trace adds a piece to the late piano tradition), <code>power</code> (Loss of Power: a lift fault on every car at 07:40, the first time you board a lift after your first meal, for four ship hours; while you're stuck, nothing counts as missed work: <code>playerShiftOn</code>'s missed-shift note and the reputation loss for unfinished jobs are skipped, jobs stay claimable; a meeting in the car if you're in it, else help from outside; Nell is an everyday guest that week, from the crew designer), <code>creature</code> (Day 8, 07:00-18:40: power dips; a hull glow on the windows; the weaning is a tune-style job on a conduit, four steps), <code>inspector</code> (a guest for one day, Day 25; her questions are a meeting; she reads the team job's result; findings by department at 16:00).</li>
    <li><code>bridgeInvite</code>: due the morning after the first event you helped in (the storm's: Day 7), for the next bridge hour (Day 23); not the day before as now.</li>
    <li>Injuries: a <code>hurt</code> rule for one named crew member per danger event (a day or two in the infirmary, the sim's sick-bay schedule); never the player.</li>
    <li>Rotation day reads <code>ROSTER_ROTATIONS</code>' first entry (Day 35); Ilse leaves with it.</li>
    <li>Pillar 5's sub-blocks: none changes. The inspector reads M24's team job result (<code>simNote('team')</code>) and the logbook (M12) if they exist, typeof-guarded.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="clash">
  <h2>Clashes found</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The storm on Pillar 5's busy Days 4-5:</b> kept, as the user says; a storm fault can be your scanner's first real use on Day 5.</li>
    <li><b>Day 2's comet</b> is in Pillar 4's first week (rounds, the health check, your first laundry): it's a quiet 21:00 evening that asks nothing of you. If it feels crowded, Day 3's evening works too (a question).</li>
    <li><b>Space Creature on Day 8</b> shares the day with your first small incident (M6) and your uniform (M2): the weaning jobs are optional and short, and it lets go at 18:40, leaving the evening and night before the test job.</li>
    <li><b>Day 24's morning</b> is the reactor permit (M23's lesson with Torres): Loss of Power takes the morning, so the permit waits for the afternoon (the ladder already waits for you; no day moves). The inspector watching your team job on Day 25 makes M24 matter more rather than adding a job.</li>
    <li><b>Missing work while stuck:</b> today a missed shift or an unfinished job can cost reputation (the 0.61.x time clock and Pillar 5's bands); Loss of Power switches that off for its four hours (the engine note above).</li>
    <li><b>The visit's Saturday is Captain's Day</b> (holidays, on hold): if holidays return, Captain's Day moves (Day 34 or 41). <b>Odd Socks Day</b> (24) would share Loss of Power's day (the lift full of odd socks: harmless). <b>Relay Day</b> (52) falls in the cough.</li>
    <li><b>Talent night</b> is Day 14 (the rec dec plan): the Veyli come to it.</li>
    <li><b>The distress call</b> is the Sunday after the night shift; the beacon is at 11:30 so you wake to it.</li>
    <li><b>The storm ends on Friday:</b> its party is the Friday jam, not film night; Saturday's film night is still the first in the auditorium, as the rec dec plan says, just not a storm event.</li>
    <li><b>Loss of Power needs a child aboard:</b> Nell comes as an everyday guest with her parent that week (the crew designer's guests).</li>
    <li><b>Stowaway and the garden creature:</b> the stowaway is a person; the garden creature comes from the crates of a delivery (or salvage, in later playthroughs).</li>
    <li><b>Space Creature and reactor trouble</b> both dip the power: eight weeks apart, and different (a gentle drain; a precaution at half power).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="q">
  <h2>Open questions for the user (with my recommendations)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>The comet on Day 2 or Day 3?</b> Day 2 is your first proper day of rounds. <i>Recommended: Day 2; it's an evening, and it introduces Sato before her storm.</i></li>
    <li><b>The inspector watching your first team job as lead</b> (Day 25)? <i>Recommended: yes; it makes the inspection about your real work. A small nudge, if wanted: M24 could move to Day 24 so the inspector sees a normal day (I'd keep it as is).</i></li>
    <li><b>Loss of Power's group:</b> Brennan, Nell and Commander Vance? <i>Recommended: yes (Holt instead of Vance would be funnier, but Vance's story is the heart of it).</i></li>
    <li><b>Getting you into the lift:</b> the first lift you take after your first meal (someone calls "Hold the doors!"). <i>Recommended: yes; if you never ride one that morning, you help from outside.</i></li>
    <li><b>The creature's name:</b> a crew vote with your suggestion in it ("Sprat" leads). <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
    <li><b>The inspector's findings:</b> read out in a meeting, plus a Mail. <i>Recommended: yes, short and kind.</i></li>
    <li><b>Halden</b> (Echo Signal): a mystery, a seed for the story pillar. <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
    <li><b>After the last event (Day 100):</b> nothing more until later pillars? <i>Recommended: yes, as "never repeat" says.</i></li>
      <li><b>Space Creature's day (short):</b> "a day earlier" would put it in your free first weekend, so v4 makes it <b>Day 8 alone</b>, gone by 18:40, which leaves the evening and night before the Day 9 test. Or: Day 7 (Sunday), if a cozy event on the weekend is fine. <i>Recommended: Day 8 alone, as here.</i></li>
</ol>
</section>
